S141 LRC14 REGULAR-SOLID / EUCLIDEAN-TILING RECURSION CARRIER
==============================================================================
[1] Assumption challenge / quotient declaration
  considered vertices:
    regular tiling cells, tiling vertex figures, Platonic/Archimedean
    vertex configurations, prism/antiprism annuli, Johnson defect packets,
    q=3 unital points, C27 shells, and LRC proof obligations.
  chosen predicate:
    normalized angle defect kappa = 1 - sum interior_angle/(2*pi),
    plus declared self/dual recursion counts.
  quotient preserves:
    local curvature/defect, duality type, self-recursion count, finite
    atlas status, and whether a carrier has the LRC 1/14 defect scale.
  quotient destroys:
    exact LRC time geometry, exact denominator witnesses, and pair
    incidence unless the q=3 unital layer is separately attached.
  challenged assumption:
    Platonic/Archimedean/Johnson solids form one global atlas.  The audit
    splits them into uniform curvature laws, annular 14/28 carriers, and
    finite nonuniform Johnson defect packets.

